WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
I think in the UK, people are just
sort of reckoning now with

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.960
the existence of anti-Semitism
and I think that,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.600
that sort of self-interrogation
is very difficult for people.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.000
I think it's an identity crisis in
the UK - people understanding

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.840
that anti-Semitism
does in fact exist.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.920
I have experienced anti-Semitism
from people who are on the far left

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.720
and the far right, and people who are
black and white, men and women.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.400
Anti-Semitism is not restricted
to one party or gender or race.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.240
Anti-Semitism is for everybody.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.000
This is a news clip
from the late-1950s.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.240
A swastika got painted
on a synagogue in Leeds.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.080
Finally, are you worried?

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.760
No, not in the least, there's
nothing to be worried about -

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.200
one ignores these things.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.520
I think that’s so British,
to just be Iike,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.920
"Yes, there's nothing to worry about,
one ignores these things."

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.440
But I also think that's
sort of the reason that...

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.520
The vast majority of people
are not actively anti-Semitic.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.280
And when anti-Semitic stuff
like that did happen,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.200
and for many years when it has
happened, it's sort of like,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.080
"Oh well, we'll wash it off the wall
and get on with business as usual."

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.160
And now that it's back in the
forefront, I think it's shocking for

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.520
people precisely because
it is the kind of thing that

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.560
you would move past.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.520
It's so interesting to watch this,
because this feels like

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.320
1930's rhetoric.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.440
This Orban speech sums up
so much of anti-Semitic rhetoric,

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.400
because he says,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.160
"Not open, but hiding.
Not straightforward, but crafty."

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.720
And then he goes,
"Not national, but international."

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.400
It's that tie between
nationalism and anti-Semitism

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.800
that Jews are somehow not from here -
they don't belong here.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.880
They're part of this global cabal,

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.640
that's here to
take stuff away from us.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.640
And always the crafty thing.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.400
There's no way to describe Jews
that doesn't sound ludicrous

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.360
when they go into sort of
that stereotype they're like,

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.560
"They're crafty" or "They're sneaky"
"They're wily."

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.520
I think Jews get bludgeoned
with Israel sometimes.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.720
I think Israel is like a very weird
lead pipe for a lot of people

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.600
they're just like, 

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.200
"Well, you're Jewish,
so explain this Israeli policy."

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.920
And you're like, "Well, I don't know
if I 100% agree with that policy,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.040
because, you know...

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.400
And they're like, "Well, then do
you think Israel shouldn't exist?"

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.680
And you're like, "Well no.
That's not what I said either."

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.840
Israel is a very complicated issue,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.160
and it is the only sort of
Jewish homeland on earth

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:12.440
so for that reason, Jews do have
a special affiliation with it.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:18.160
And it is a place, by the way,
where I love my time in Israel,

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.080
because it is one of the only
places where I do not feel

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.320
othered for being Jewish.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.400
I've taken issue with many of its
policies in the same way that

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.160
I take issue with many of the UK's
policies and many American policies.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.760
But I do think...

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.320
...or it's used to
justify anti-Semitism.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.440
My favorite quote about anti-Semitism
is this Jean-Paul Sartre quote,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.360
which is that...

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.840
...and I think about that
all the time.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.800
I do think that a good way
to reduce anti-Semitism

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.720
is for people to understand
that Jew is a label

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.560
or Jew as a type is a label
that is entirely constructed.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:09.440
It doesn't mean that you are a
type of person or a certain way.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:14.160
There is a strong heritage which you
may opt into if you so choose.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.600
I think it's crucial for people to
understand that Jews are complicated

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.520
in the same way that
everybody else is.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.880
There are rich Jews and poor Jews,
and Jews who are educated,

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:25.840
and Jews who are not.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.360
And if you think all Jews are sort
of powerful and educated and rich,

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.160
I have a bunch of cousins
that you should meet,

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.000
because it's not the case. 

